  "hash": "e368fa3275b2912a0541121b87053a9c",
  "result": {
    "engine": "knitr",
    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Converting REDCap branching logic into R\"\nauthor: \"Ben Harrap\"\ndate: 2026-07-08\ntoc: true\ncategories:\n  - programming\n  - R\n  - REDCap\n---\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n\nIn cleaning a dataset, I encode information about data missingness. One such category of missingness is \"not asked\", for questions that were not displayed to participants due to their response to an earlier question.\n\nIf you use REDCap to gather data, the conditions used to control the display of questions are called \"branching logic\". REDCap provides details of the branching logic in the data dictionary, which we can use to automate the encoding of this missingness category!\n\n## Step 0: Use the REDCap API\n\nIf you're not using the REDCap API to access the data, let me introduce you to the [REDCapR package](https://ouhscbbmc.github.io/REDCapR/). The key functions we will use are:\n\n- `redcap_read()` to access data\n- `redcap_read_metadata()` to access the data dictionary\n\nThis saves you having to repeatedly download the data and dictionary and avoids you storing data locally.\n\nLet's pretend we have the following dataset:\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\ndata <- tibble(\n  record_id = c(1,2,3,4,5),\n  age = c(16,18,20,24,26),\n  has_pets = c(1,0,1,1,0),\n  pet_rating = c(1,NA,2,1,NA),\n  pet_insurance = c(NA,0,1,0,1)\n) |> \n  mutate(across(!record_id, as.character))\ntt(data)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<!-- preamble start -->\n\n    <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/vincentarelbundock/tinytable@main/inst/tinytable.js\"></script>\n\n    <script>\n      // Create table-specific functions using external factory\n      const tableFns_p74yz8119cijzvbnxct9 = TinyTable.createTableFunctions(\"tinytable_p74yz8119cijzvbnxct9\");\n      // tinytable span after\n      window.addEventListener('load', function () {\n          var cellsToStyle = [\n            // tinytable style arrays after\n          { positions: [ { i: '5', j: 1 }, { i: '5', j: 2 }, { i: '5', j: 3 }, { i: '5', j: 4 }, { i: '5', j: 5 } ], css_id: 'tinytable_css_rmkn7irsilhrev0o2dpq',}, \n          { positions: [ { i: '0', j: 1 }, { i: '0', j: 2 }, { i: '0', j: 3 }, { i: '0', j: 4 }, { i: '0', j: 5 } ], css_id: 'tinytable_css_3obtnsa3738u7xmqy4o6',}, \n          ];\n\n          // Loop over the arrays to style the cells\n          cellsToStyle.forEach(function (group) {\n              group.positions.forEach(function (cell) {\n                  tableFns_p74yz8119cijzvbnxct9.styleCell(cell.i, cell.j, group.css_id);\n              });\n          });\n      });\n    </script>\n\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/vincentarelbundock/tinytable@main/inst/tinytable.css\">\n    <style>\n    /* tinytable css entries after */\n    #tinytable_p74yz8119cijzvbnxct9 td.tinytable_css_rmkn7irsilhrev0o2dpq, #tinytable_p74yz8119cijzvbnxct9 th.tinytable_css_rmkn7irsilhrev0o2dpq {  position: relative; --border-bottom: 1; --border-left: 0; --border-right: 0; --border-top: 0; --line-color-bottom: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-left: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-right: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-top: var(--tt-line-color); --line-width-bottom: 0.08em; --line-width-left: 0.1em; --line-width-right: 0.1em; --line-width-top: 0.1em; --trim-bottom-left: 0%; --trim-bottom-right: 0%; --trim-left-bottom: 0%; --trim-left-top: 0%; --trim-right-bottom: 0%; --trim-right-top: 0%; --trim-top-left: 0%; --trim-top-right: 0%;  }\n    #tinytable_p74yz8119cijzvbnxct9 td.tinytable_css_3obtnsa3738u7xmqy4o6, #tinytable_p74yz8119cijzvbnxct9 th.tinytable_css_3obtnsa3738u7xmqy4o6 {  position: relative; --border-bottom: 1; --border-left: 0; --border-right: 0; --border-top: 1; --line-color-bottom: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-left: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-right: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-top: var(--tt-line-color); --line-width-bottom: 0.05em; --line-width-left: 0.1em; --line-width-right: 0.1em; --line-width-top: 0.08em; --trim-bottom-left: 0%; --trim-bottom-right: 0%; --trim-left-bottom: 0%; --trim-left-top: 0%; --trim-right-bottom: 0%; --trim-right-top: 0%; --trim-top-left: 0%; --trim-top-right: 0%;  }\n    </style>\n    <div class=\"container\">\n      <table class=\"tinytable\" id=\"tinytable_p74yz8119cijzvbnxct9\" style=\"width: auto; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" data-quarto-disable-processing='true'>\n        \n        <thead>\n              <tr>\n                <th scope=\"col\" data-row=\"0\" data-col=\"1\">record_id</th>\n                <th scope=\"col\" data-row=\"0\" data-col=\"2\">age</th>\n                <th scope=\"col\" data-row=\"0\" data-col=\"3\">has_pets</th>\n                <th scope=\"col\" data-row=\"0\" data-col=\"4\">pet_rating</th>\n                <th scope=\"col\" data-row=\"0\" data-col=\"5\">pet_insurance</th>\n              </tr>\n        </thead>\n        \n        <tbody>\n                <tr>\n                  <td data-row=\"1\" data-col=\"1\">1</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"1\" data-col=\"2\">16</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"1\" data-col=\"3\">1</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"1\" data-col=\"4\">1</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"1\" data-col=\"5\">NA</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <td data-row=\"2\" data-col=\"1\">2</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"2\" data-col=\"2\">18</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"2\" data-col=\"3\">0</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"2\" data-col=\"4\">NA</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"2\" data-col=\"5\">0</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <td data-row=\"3\" data-col=\"1\">3</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"3\" data-col=\"2\">20</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"3\" data-col=\"3\">1</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"3\" data-col=\"4\">2</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"3\" data-col=\"5\">1</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <td data-row=\"4\" data-col=\"1\">4</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"4\" data-col=\"2\">24</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"4\" data-col=\"3\">1</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"4\" data-col=\"4\">1</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"4\" data-col=\"5\">0</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <td data-row=\"5\" data-col=\"1\">5</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"5\" data-col=\"2\">26</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"5\" data-col=\"3\">0</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"5\" data-col=\"4\">NA</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"5\" data-col=\"5\">1</td>\n                </tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n<!-- hack to avoid NA insertion in last line -->\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\nEverything is a character at this point, which is relevant to be able to use `dplyr::rows_update()` later on.\n\nWe also have this dictionary from REDCap, noting this is only a few of the columns that REDCap provides:\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\ndictionary <- tibble(\n  field_name = c(\"record_id\", \"age\", \"has_pets\", \"pet_rating\",\"pet_insurance\"),\n  field_type = c(\"text\", \"text\", \"yesno\", \"radio\",\"yesno\"),\n  branching_logic = c(NA,NA,NA,\"[has_pets] = '1'\",\"[has_pets] = '1' and [age] >= '18'\")\n)\ntt(dictionary)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<!-- preamble start -->\n\n    <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/vincentarelbundock/tinytable@main/inst/tinytable.js\"></script>\n\n    <script>\n      // Create table-specific functions using external factory\n      const tableFns_fh78rpp0ma6dope7wyzt = TinyTable.createTableFunctions(\"tinytable_fh78rpp0ma6dope7wyzt\");\n      // tinytable span after\n      window.addEventListener('load', function () {\n          var cellsToStyle = [\n            // tinytable style arrays after\n          { positions: [ { i: '5', j: 1 }, { i: '5', j: 2 }, { i: '5', j: 3 } ], css_id: 'tinytable_css_xiz7zqy0ib04p95q888l',}, \n          { positions: [ { i: '0', j: 1 }, { i: '0', j: 2 }, { i: '0', j: 3 } ], css_id: 'tinytable_css_ny0yozaapbq2qc78c03j',}, \n          ];\n\n          // Loop over the arrays to style the cells\n          cellsToStyle.forEach(function (group) {\n              group.positions.forEach(function (cell) {\n                  tableFns_fh78rpp0ma6dope7wyzt.styleCell(cell.i, cell.j, group.css_id);\n              });\n          });\n      });\n    </script>\n\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/vincentarelbundock/tinytable@main/inst/tinytable.css\">\n    <style>\n    /* tinytable css entries after */\n    #tinytable_fh78rpp0ma6dope7wyzt td.tinytable_css_xiz7zqy0ib04p95q888l, #tinytable_fh78rpp0ma6dope7wyzt th.tinytable_css_xiz7zqy0ib04p95q888l {  position: relative; --border-bottom: 1; --border-left: 0; --border-right: 0; --border-top: 0; --line-color-bottom: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-left: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-right: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-top: var(--tt-line-color); --line-width-bottom: 0.08em; --line-width-left: 0.1em; --line-width-right: 0.1em; --line-width-top: 0.1em; --trim-bottom-left: 0%; --trim-bottom-right: 0%; --trim-left-bottom: 0%; --trim-left-top: 0%; --trim-right-bottom: 0%; --trim-right-top: 0%; --trim-top-left: 0%; --trim-top-right: 0%;  }\n    #tinytable_fh78rpp0ma6dope7wyzt td.tinytable_css_ny0yozaapbq2qc78c03j, #tinytable_fh78rpp0ma6dope7wyzt th.tinytable_css_ny0yozaapbq2qc78c03j {  position: relative; --border-bottom: 1; --border-left: 0; --border-right: 0; --border-top: 1; --line-color-bottom: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-left: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-right: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-top: var(--tt-line-color); --line-width-bottom: 0.05em; --line-width-left: 0.1em; --line-width-right: 0.1em; --line-width-top: 0.08em; --trim-bottom-left: 0%; --trim-bottom-right: 0%; --trim-left-bottom: 0%; --trim-left-top: 0%; --trim-right-bottom: 0%; --trim-right-top: 0%; --trim-top-left: 0%; --trim-top-right: 0%;  }\n    </style>\n    <div class=\"container\">\n      <table class=\"tinytable\" id=\"tinytable_fh78rpp0ma6dope7wyzt\" style=\"width: auto; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" data-quarto-disable-processing='true'>\n        \n        <thead>\n              <tr>\n                <th scope=\"col\" data-row=\"0\" data-col=\"1\">field_name</th>\n                <th scope=\"col\" data-row=\"0\" data-col=\"2\">field_type</th>\n                <th scope=\"col\" data-row=\"0\" data-col=\"3\">branching_logic</th>\n              </tr>\n        </thead>\n        \n        <tbody>\n                <tr>\n                  <td data-row=\"1\" data-col=\"1\">record_id</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"1\" data-col=\"2\">text</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"1\" data-col=\"3\">NA</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <td data-row=\"2\" data-col=\"1\">age</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"2\" data-col=\"2\">text</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"2\" data-col=\"3\">NA</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <td data-row=\"3\" data-col=\"1\">has_pets</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"3\" data-col=\"2\">yesno</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"3\" data-col=\"3\">NA</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <td data-row=\"4\" data-col=\"1\">pet_rating</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"4\" data-col=\"2\">radio</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"4\" data-col=\"3\">[has_pets] = '1'</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <td data-row=\"5\" data-col=\"1\">pet_insurance</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"5\" data-col=\"2\">yesno</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"5\" data-col=\"3\">[has_pets] = '1' and [age] >= '18'</td>\n                </tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n<!-- hack to avoid NA insertion in last line -->\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\nWith the data and dictionary read in to the environment, we can start step 1.\n\n## Step 1: Convert branching logic\n\n### Anatomy of REDCap branching logic\n\nLet's look at the branching logic for `pet_rating`, where `has_pets` must be `1` for the question to be shown.\n\n```\n[has_pets] = '1'\n```\n\nA variable (or field name as REDCap calls it) is always referred to using square brackets. This is true for every variable except for checkboxes, which also incorporate round brackets. I won't go into checkboxes here — they're annoying and require extra data cleaning.\n\nOnce you start combining conditions, REDCap uses brackets as you might expect. If the branching logic wanted to target people aged outside of 18 to 25 who have pets it would be:\n\n```\n([age] < '18' or [age] > '25') and [has_pets] = '1'\n```\n\n### Parlez vous R, REDCap? \n\nNow we understand the anatomy of REDCap branching logic, let's compare how operators are expressed in REDCap vs. R:\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<!-- preamble start -->\n\n    <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/vincentarelbundock/tinytable@main/inst/tinytable.js\"></script>\n\n    <script>\n      // Create table-specific functions using external factory\n      const tableFns_fpgxc6qyd9ipy6o8pdab = TinyTable.createTableFunctions(\"tinytable_fpgxc6qyd9ipy6o8pdab\");\n      // tinytable span after\n      window.addEventListener('load', function () {\n          var cellsToStyle = [\n            // tinytable style arrays after\n          { positions: [ { i: '8', j: 1 }, { i: '8', j: 2 }, { i: '8', j: 3 } ], css_id: 'tinytable_css_66ng4626fvq3xujdyv2w',}, \n          { positions: [ { i: '0', j: 1 }, { i: '0', j: 2 }, { i: '0', j: 3 } ], css_id: 'tinytable_css_7tyd8qwag9hdjriyvslj',}, \n          ];\n\n          // Loop over the arrays to style the cells\n          cellsToStyle.forEach(function (group) {\n              group.positions.forEach(function (cell) {\n                  tableFns_fpgxc6qyd9ipy6o8pdab.styleCell(cell.i, cell.j, group.css_id);\n              });\n          });\n      });\n    </script>\n\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/vincentarelbundock/tinytable@main/inst/tinytable.css\">\n    <style>\n    /* tinytable css entries after */\n    #tinytable_fpgxc6qyd9ipy6o8pdab td.tinytable_css_66ng4626fvq3xujdyv2w, #tinytable_fpgxc6qyd9ipy6o8pdab th.tinytable_css_66ng4626fvq3xujdyv2w {  position: relative; --border-bottom: 1; --border-left: 0; --border-right: 0; --border-top: 0; --line-color-bottom: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-left: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-right: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-top: var(--tt-line-color); --line-width-bottom: 0.08em; --line-width-left: 0.1em; --line-width-right: 0.1em; --line-width-top: 0.1em; --trim-bottom-left: 0%; --trim-bottom-right: 0%; --trim-left-bottom: 0%; --trim-left-top: 0%; --trim-right-bottom: 0%; --trim-right-top: 0%; --trim-top-left: 0%; --trim-top-right: 0%;  }\n    #tinytable_fpgxc6qyd9ipy6o8pdab td.tinytable_css_7tyd8qwag9hdjriyvslj, #tinytable_fpgxc6qyd9ipy6o8pdab th.tinytable_css_7tyd8qwag9hdjriyvslj {  position: relative; --border-bottom: 1; --border-left: 0; --border-right: 0; --border-top: 1; --line-color-bottom: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-left: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-right: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-top: var(--tt-line-color); --line-width-bottom: 0.05em; --line-width-left: 0.1em; --line-width-right: 0.1em; --line-width-top: 0.08em; --trim-bottom-left: 0%; --trim-bottom-right: 0%; --trim-left-bottom: 0%; --trim-left-top: 0%; --trim-right-bottom: 0%; --trim-right-top: 0%; --trim-top-left: 0%; --trim-top-right: 0%;  }\n    </style>\n    <div class=\"container\">\n      <table class=\"tinytable\" id=\"tinytable_fpgxc6qyd9ipy6o8pdab\" style=\"width: auto; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" data-quarto-disable-processing='true'>\n        \n        <thead>\n              <tr>\n                <th scope=\"col\" data-row=\"0\" data-col=\"1\">Operator</th>\n                <th scope=\"col\" data-row=\"0\" data-col=\"2\">REDCap</th>\n                <th scope=\"col\" data-row=\"0\" data-col=\"3\">R</th>\n              </tr>\n        </thead>\n        \n        <tbody>\n                <tr>\n                  <td data-row=\"1\" data-col=\"1\">Greater than</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"1\" data-col=\"2\">></td>\n                  <td data-row=\"1\" data-col=\"3\">></td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <td data-row=\"2\" data-col=\"1\">Greater than or equals</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"2\" data-col=\"2\">>=</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"2\" data-col=\"3\">>=</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <td data-row=\"3\" data-col=\"1\">Less than</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"3\" data-col=\"2\"><</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"3\" data-col=\"3\"><</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <td data-row=\"4\" data-col=\"1\">Less than or equals</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"4\" data-col=\"2\"><=</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"4\" data-col=\"3\"><=</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <td data-row=\"5\" data-col=\"1\">Equal</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"5\" data-col=\"2\">=</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"5\" data-col=\"3\">==</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <td data-row=\"6\" data-col=\"1\">Not equal</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"6\" data-col=\"2\"><></td>\n                  <td data-row=\"6\" data-col=\"3\">!=</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <td data-row=\"7\" data-col=\"1\">And</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"7\" data-col=\"2\">and</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"7\" data-col=\"3\">&</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <td data-row=\"8\" data-col=\"1\">Or</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"8\" data-col=\"2\">or</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"8\" data-col=\"3\">|</td>\n                </tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n<!-- hack to avoid NA insertion in last line -->\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\nNote that `==`, `!=`, `&` and `|` are not the same.\n\n### Nein, ich spreche R nicht\n\nWith our knowledge of how REDCap expresses variables and operators, we now need to translate into Rspeak.\n\nFortunately, this is made straightforward thanks to `stringr::str_replace_all()`\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\ndictionary <- dictionary |>\n    mutate(\n      converted_logic = str_replace_all(\n        branching_logic,\n        c(\n          \" and \" = \" & \", # <1>\n          \" or \" = \" \\\\| \", # <1>\n          \"\\\\[([[:alnum:]_]+)\\\\] = ''\" = \"is.na(\\\\1)\", # <2>\n          \"\\\\[([[:alnum:]_]+)\\\\] <> ''\" = \"!is.na(\\\\1)\", # <2>\n          \" <> \" = \" != \", # <3>\n          \" = \" = \" == \", # <3>\n          \"\\\\(1\\\\)\\\\]\" = \"\", # <4>\n          \"\\\\[\" = \"\", # <5>\n          \"\\\\]\" = \"\" # <5>\n        )\n      )\n    )\n```\n:::\n\n\n1. Note the pipe `|` needs to be escaped and that the spaces around `and` and `or` are intentional. REDCap requires spaces around these operators and by incorporating the spaces in the pattern we won't accidentally target a variable that has `and` or `or` in its name\n2. Instances where the branching logic looks for missing data are handled next, to prevent them being handled in parts 4 and 5. We're targeting any combination of letters/numbers `[:alnum:]` and underscores contained within square brackets, that are followed by (not) equals to missing `''`. By making use of regex groups `\\\\1`, if there are multiple conditions based on missingness within the same branching logic, they'll all be handled.\n3. Convert the remaining equals and not equals operators\n4. This step targets how checkboxes are expressed in branching logic. It might depend on how you clean/name your variables, but I've included it as I ended up using it for my context.\n5. Remove remaining square brackets.\n\nThe code annotations above explain each of the steps, but you can see the result below\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<!-- preamble start -->\n\n    <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/vincentarelbundock/tinytable@main/inst/tinytable.js\"></script>\n\n    <script>\n      // Create table-specific functions using external factory\n      const tableFns_1cry7apwjt9oigk2b91u = TinyTable.createTableFunctions(\"tinytable_1cry7apwjt9oigk2b91u\");\n      // tinytable span after\n      window.addEventListener('load', function () {\n          var cellsToStyle = [\n            // tinytable style arrays after\n          { positions: [ { i: '5', j: 1 }, { i: '5', j: 2 }, { i: '5', j: 3 }, { i: '5', j: 4 } ], css_id: 'tinytable_css_0kumap3li9a76elp5dc2',}, \n          { positions: [ { i: '0', j: 1 }, { i: '0', j: 2 }, { i: '0', j: 3 }, { i: '0', j: 4 } ], css_id: 'tinytable_css_uiob3wn37bte1hl03x7s',}, \n          ];\n\n          // Loop over the arrays to style the cells\n          cellsToStyle.forEach(function (group) {\n              group.positions.forEach(function (cell) {\n                  tableFns_1cry7apwjt9oigk2b91u.styleCell(cell.i, cell.j, group.css_id);\n              });\n          });\n      });\n    </script>\n\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/vincentarelbundock/tinytable@main/inst/tinytable.css\">\n    <style>\n    /* tinytable css entries after */\n    #tinytable_1cry7apwjt9oigk2b91u td.tinytable_css_0kumap3li9a76elp5dc2, #tinytable_1cry7apwjt9oigk2b91u th.tinytable_css_0kumap3li9a76elp5dc2 {  position: relative; --border-bottom: 1; --border-left: 0; --border-right: 0; --border-top: 0; --line-color-bottom: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-left: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-right: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-top: var(--tt-line-color); --line-width-bottom: 0.08em; --line-width-left: 0.1em; --line-width-right: 0.1em; --line-width-top: 0.1em; --trim-bottom-left: 0%; --trim-bottom-right: 0%; --trim-left-bottom: 0%; --trim-left-top: 0%; --trim-right-bottom: 0%; --trim-right-top: 0%; --trim-top-left: 0%; --trim-top-right: 0%;  }\n    #tinytable_1cry7apwjt9oigk2b91u td.tinytable_css_uiob3wn37bte1hl03x7s, #tinytable_1cry7apwjt9oigk2b91u th.tinytable_css_uiob3wn37bte1hl03x7s {  position: relative; --border-bottom: 1; --border-left: 0; --border-right: 0; --border-top: 1; --line-color-bottom: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-left: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-right: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-top: var(--tt-line-color); --line-width-bottom: 0.05em; --line-width-left: 0.1em; --line-width-right: 0.1em; --line-width-top: 0.08em; --trim-bottom-left: 0%; --trim-bottom-right: 0%; --trim-left-bottom: 0%; --trim-left-top: 0%; --trim-right-bottom: 0%; --trim-right-top: 0%; --trim-top-left: 0%; --trim-top-right: 0%;  }\n    </style>\n    <div class=\"container\">\n      <table class=\"tinytable\" id=\"tinytable_1cry7apwjt9oigk2b91u\" style=\"width: auto; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" data-quarto-disable-processing='true'>\n        \n        <thead>\n              <tr>\n                <th scope=\"col\" data-row=\"0\" data-col=\"1\">field_name</th>\n                <th scope=\"col\" data-row=\"0\" data-col=\"2\">field_type</th>\n                <th scope=\"col\" data-row=\"0\" data-col=\"3\">branching_logic</th>\n                <th scope=\"col\" data-row=\"0\" data-col=\"4\">converted_logic</th>\n              </tr>\n        </thead>\n        \n        <tbody>\n                <tr>\n                  <td data-row=\"1\" data-col=\"1\">record_id</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"1\" data-col=\"2\">text</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"1\" data-col=\"3\">NA</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"1\" data-col=\"4\">NA</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <td data-row=\"2\" data-col=\"1\">age</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"2\" data-col=\"2\">text</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"2\" data-col=\"3\">NA</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"2\" data-col=\"4\">NA</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <td data-row=\"3\" data-col=\"1\">has_pets</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"3\" data-col=\"2\">yesno</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"3\" data-col=\"3\">NA</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"3\" data-col=\"4\">NA</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <td data-row=\"4\" data-col=\"1\">pet_rating</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"4\" data-col=\"2\">radio</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"4\" data-col=\"3\">[has_pets] = '1'</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"4\" data-col=\"4\">has_pets == '1'</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <td data-row=\"5\" data-col=\"1\">pet_insurance</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"5\" data-col=\"2\">yesno</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"5\" data-col=\"3\">[has_pets] = '1' and [age] >= '18'</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"5\" data-col=\"4\">has_pets == '1' & age >= '18'</td>\n                </tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n<!-- hack to avoid NA insertion in last line -->\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Step 2: Parse the converted logic as code\n\nBefore we use the logic, we need to do one more step. The branching logic as it currently stands will be `TRUE` if the criteria are met, which means the question *was* asked. We care about the question *not* being asked, and we also want to make sure we're only going to affect observations with missing data.\n\nTo reflect this, we just need to add an `is.na()` condition and invert the converted logic expression using `!()`\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nbranching_logic <- dictionary |> \n  filter(!is.na(branching_logic)) |> \n  mutate(\n    not_asked = paste0(\"is.na(\", field_name, \") & !(\", converted_logic, \")\")\n  ) |> \n  select(field_name, not_asked)\n\ntt(branching_logic)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<!-- preamble start -->\n\n    <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/vincentarelbundock/tinytable@main/inst/tinytable.js\"></script>\n\n    <script>\n      // Create table-specific functions using external factory\n      const tableFns_no4iky8i0bd2sgnptqwm = TinyTable.createTableFunctions(\"tinytable_no4iky8i0bd2sgnptqwm\");\n      // tinytable span after\n      window.addEventListener('load', function () {\n          var cellsToStyle = [\n            // tinytable style arrays after\n          { positions: [ { i: '2', j: 1 }, { i: '2', j: 2 } ], css_id: 'tinytable_css_88h9in6sf9jczbdd40s9',}, \n          { positions: [ { i: '0', j: 1 }, { i: '0', j: 2 } ], css_id: 'tinytable_css_ws6okzcp9inkd71kd5fv',}, \n          ];\n\n          // Loop over the arrays to style the cells\n          cellsToStyle.forEach(function (group) {\n              group.positions.forEach(function (cell) {\n                  tableFns_no4iky8i0bd2sgnptqwm.styleCell(cell.i, cell.j, group.css_id);\n              });\n          });\n      });\n    </script>\n\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/vincentarelbundock/tinytable@main/inst/tinytable.css\">\n    <style>\n    /* tinytable css entries after */\n    #tinytable_no4iky8i0bd2sgnptqwm td.tinytable_css_88h9in6sf9jczbdd40s9, #tinytable_no4iky8i0bd2sgnptqwm th.tinytable_css_88h9in6sf9jczbdd40s9 {  position: relative; --border-bottom: 1; --border-left: 0; --border-right: 0; --border-top: 0; --line-color-bottom: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-left: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-right: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-top: var(--tt-line-color); --line-width-bottom: 0.08em; --line-width-left: 0.1em; --line-width-right: 0.1em; --line-width-top: 0.1em; --trim-bottom-left: 0%; --trim-bottom-right: 0%; --trim-left-bottom: 0%; --trim-left-top: 0%; --trim-right-bottom: 0%; --trim-right-top: 0%; --trim-top-left: 0%; --trim-top-right: 0%;  }\n    #tinytable_no4iky8i0bd2sgnptqwm td.tinytable_css_ws6okzcp9inkd71kd5fv, #tinytable_no4iky8i0bd2sgnptqwm th.tinytable_css_ws6okzcp9inkd71kd5fv {  position: relative; --border-bottom: 1; --border-left: 0; --border-right: 0; --border-top: 1; --line-color-bottom: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-left: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-right: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-top: var(--tt-line-color); --line-width-bottom: 0.05em; --line-width-left: 0.1em; --line-width-right: 0.1em; --line-width-top: 0.08em; --trim-bottom-left: 0%; --trim-bottom-right: 0%; --trim-left-bottom: 0%; --trim-left-top: 0%; --trim-right-bottom: 0%; --trim-right-top: 0%; --trim-top-left: 0%; --trim-top-right: 0%;  }\n    </style>\n    <div class=\"container\">\n      <table class=\"tinytable\" id=\"tinytable_no4iky8i0bd2sgnptqwm\" style=\"width: auto; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" data-quarto-disable-processing='true'>\n        \n        <thead>\n              <tr>\n                <th scope=\"col\" data-row=\"0\" data-col=\"1\">field_name</th>\n                <th scope=\"col\" data-row=\"0\" data-col=\"2\">not_asked</th>\n              </tr>\n        </thead>\n        \n        <tbody>\n                <tr>\n                  <td data-row=\"1\" data-col=\"1\">pet_rating</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"1\" data-col=\"2\">is.na(pet_rating) & !(has_pets == '1')</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <td data-row=\"2\" data-col=\"1\">pet_insurance</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"2\" data-col=\"2\">is.na(pet_insurance) & !(has_pets == '1' & age >= '18')</td>\n                </tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n<!-- hack to avoid NA insertion in last line -->\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\nNow we have the code in a format acceptable to R, we can use [`rlang::parse_expr()`](https://rlang.r-lib.org/reference/parse_expr.html) to execute the strings as code.\n\nSince I'm iterating over many columns in my dataset, I wrote a function to return the rows that need to have their missing data encoded:\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nrecords_not_asked <- function(uncoded_data, column){\n    logic <- branching_logic |> \n      # Keep just the variable of interest\n      filter(field_name == column) |> \n      # Pull out the logic\n      pull(not_asked)\n    \n    uncoded_data |> \n      # Apply the logic to the input data using parse_expr()\n      filter(!!parse_expr(logic)) |> \n      # Update that column to be -888888\n      mutate(\n        field_name = column,\n        value = \"-888888\") |>\n      # Return only record_id and input column\n      select(record_id, field_name, value)\n  }\n```\n:::\n\n\nThe reason for returning data in this format is because I intend to use `dplyr::rows_update()` to update the original dataset, rather than try and do all of this in one pipe.\n\n## Step 3: Find records that need updating\n\nWith the function ready to iterate over columns that have branching logic, we can use `purrr::map()` to iterate over the data\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nrecords_to_update <- bind_rows(\n  map(\n    pull(branching_logic, field_name),\n    \\(x) records_not_asked(data, x)\n  )\n)\n\ntt(records_to_update)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<!-- preamble start -->\n\n    <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/vincentarelbundock/tinytable@main/inst/tinytable.js\"></script>\n\n    <script>\n      // Create table-specific functions using external factory\n      const tableFns_ax4t1wpnl8l1f2iqrkmu = TinyTable.createTableFunctions(\"tinytable_ax4t1wpnl8l1f2iqrkmu\");\n      // tinytable span after\n      window.addEventListener('load', function () {\n          var cellsToStyle = [\n            // tinytable style arrays after\n          { positions: [ { i: '3', j: 1 }, { i: '3', j: 2 }, { i: '3', j: 3 } ], css_id: 'tinytable_css_2oz8hxfldpeymbsltofh',}, \n          { positions: [ { i: '0', j: 1 }, { i: '0', j: 2 }, { i: '0', j: 3 } ], css_id: 'tinytable_css_ief1l1vt0dzl3rtqu9rx',}, \n          ];\n\n          // Loop over the arrays to style the cells\n          cellsToStyle.forEach(function (group) {\n              group.positions.forEach(function (cell) {\n                  tableFns_ax4t1wpnl8l1f2iqrkmu.styleCell(cell.i, cell.j, group.css_id);\n              });\n          });\n      });\n    </script>\n\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/vincentarelbundock/tinytable@main/inst/tinytable.css\">\n    <style>\n    /* tinytable css entries after */\n    #tinytable_ax4t1wpnl8l1f2iqrkmu td.tinytable_css_2oz8hxfldpeymbsltofh, #tinytable_ax4t1wpnl8l1f2iqrkmu th.tinytable_css_2oz8hxfldpeymbsltofh {  position: relative; --border-bottom: 1; --border-left: 0; --border-right: 0; --border-top: 0; --line-color-bottom: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-left: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-right: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-top: var(--tt-line-color); --line-width-bottom: 0.08em; --line-width-left: 0.1em; --line-width-right: 0.1em; --line-width-top: 0.1em; --trim-bottom-left: 0%; --trim-bottom-right: 0%; --trim-left-bottom: 0%; --trim-left-top: 0%; --trim-right-bottom: 0%; --trim-right-top: 0%; --trim-top-left: 0%; --trim-top-right: 0%;  }\n    #tinytable_ax4t1wpnl8l1f2iqrkmu td.tinytable_css_ief1l1vt0dzl3rtqu9rx, #tinytable_ax4t1wpnl8l1f2iqrkmu th.tinytable_css_ief1l1vt0dzl3rtqu9rx {  position: relative; --border-bottom: 1; --border-left: 0; --border-right: 0; --border-top: 1; --line-color-bottom: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-left: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-right: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-top: var(--tt-line-color); --line-width-bottom: 0.05em; --line-width-left: 0.1em; --line-width-right: 0.1em; --line-width-top: 0.08em; --trim-bottom-left: 0%; --trim-bottom-right: 0%; --trim-left-bottom: 0%; --trim-left-top: 0%; --trim-right-bottom: 0%; --trim-right-top: 0%; --trim-top-left: 0%; --trim-top-right: 0%;  }\n    </style>\n    <div class=\"container\">\n      <table class=\"tinytable\" id=\"tinytable_ax4t1wpnl8l1f2iqrkmu\" style=\"width: auto; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" data-quarto-disable-processing='true'>\n        \n        <thead>\n              <tr>\n                <th scope=\"col\" data-row=\"0\" data-col=\"1\">record_id</th>\n                <th scope=\"col\" data-row=\"0\" data-col=\"2\">field_name</th>\n                <th scope=\"col\" data-row=\"0\" data-col=\"3\">value</th>\n              </tr>\n        </thead>\n        \n        <tbody>\n                <tr>\n                  <td data-row=\"1\" data-col=\"1\">2</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"1\" data-col=\"2\">pet_rating</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"1\" data-col=\"3\">-888888</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <td data-row=\"2\" data-col=\"1\">5</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"2\" data-col=\"2\">pet_rating</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"2\" data-col=\"3\">-888888</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <td data-row=\"3\" data-col=\"1\">1</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"3\" data-col=\"2\">pet_insurance</td>\n                  <td data-row=\"3\" data-col=\"3\">-888888</td>\n                </tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n<!-- hack to avoid NA insertion in last line -->\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Step 4: Update the records\n\nWith this list we can then safely update the values in the original dataset\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\ndata_updated <- data |> \n    pivot_longer(\n      cols = all_of(records_to_update$field_name),\n      names_to = \"field_name\",\n      values_to = \"value\"\n    ) |>\n    rows_update(records_to_update, by = c(\"record_id\", \"field_name\")) |>\n    # Reshape the updated variables back to wide format\n    pivot_wider(\n      names_from = field_name,\n      values_from = value\n    ) |>\n    # Order the variables as originally specifie